{
  "_comment": [
    "THE CONSOLE'S SNAP-INS — an MMC/RSAT-shaped view of the fleet, declared as data.",
    "",
    "WHAT MMC ACTUALLY IS, and therefore what this file models: a shell with a console TREE (scope pane), a",
    "RESULT list per node with columns, and ACTIONS per selected row. Snap-ins plug into that shell. Nothing",
    "about that needs Windows — what needs Windows is the DATA behind each node, and that already comes from",
    "the agent.",
    "",
    "WHY IT IS DATA AND NOT COMPONENTS: a snap-in here is a tree node plus columns plus actions, and every one",
    "of those is a description of something the API can already do. Written as code, each new snap-in would be",
    "a component with its own fetching, its own table and its own drift; written as data, adding 'Shares' is a",
    "block in this file. Same reason the config templates are data.",
    "",
    "NO SECOND DATA PATH — the rule that keeps this from becoming a parallel product. Every `source` points at",
    "an endpoint or a module that ALREADY serves the per-host management screens, and every `action` goes",
    "through the one tool-call endpoint. The console is a PRESENTATION, so a fix in service_facts shows up in",
    "both places or in neither. What the console adds over the per-host tabs is what MMC adds over a single",
    "computer's control panels: one tree, many hosts, uniform nodes and actions.",
    "",
    "AVAILABILITY IS THREE-VALUED, never two. A snap-in is `available`, `unavailable` WITH A REASON (the host",
    "is Linux, the role is not installed, the module is missing), or `unknown` because the host could not be",
    "asked. Hiding the unavailable ones would leave an operator wondering whether Yoloman can manage DHCP at",
    "all; showing them as broken would be a different lie.",
    "",
    "FIELDS:",
    "  requires[]        all must hold: {os_family} | {module} | {feature} (a Windows role/feature name)\n                    | {endpoint} — the node's own route must answer (for nodes served from Bossman's\n                      database rather than from the host, where no module exists to ask about)",
    "  source.kind       'endpoint' (an existing Bossman route) or 'tool' (a module call, params fixed here)",
    "  source.rows       dotted path to the row array in the response; '' means the response IS the array",
    "  columns[].badge   render the value as a state pill rather than text",
    "  actions[].tool    the module to call; {row.<field>} placeholders are filled from the selected row",
    "  actions[].confirm ask before running — for anything that changes a host",
    "  node_actions[]    actions that belong to the NODE, not to a row (\"New user…\"). The form is GENERATED\n                    from the module's own input_schema, which every agent publishes in GET /api/v1/tools —\n                    so a create dialog needs no markup here and cannot drift from what the module accepts.\n                    `prefill` sets initial values; `dry_run_first: true` makes the form open with the\n                    module's own preview switched on, so the first click shows a plan instead of a change.\n  actions[].hide_when  {field, equals}: an action that cannot apply to this row is not offered at all",
    "                       (greying out is the logical answer to an impossible action, not an error after)"
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "snapins": [
    {
      "id": "services",
      "title": "Services",
      "mmc_equivalent": "services.msc",
      "icon": "settings_applications",
      "description": "Every service registered on the host, with its state and start type.",
      "requires": [
        {
          "module": "service_facts"
        }
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "all",
          "title": "Services (local)",
          "source": {
            "kind": "endpoint",
            "path": "/api/v1/agents/{agent_id}/service-units",
            "rows": "services"
          },
          "sort": "name",
          "columns": [
            {
              "key": "name",
              "title": "Name",
              "width": 230
            },
            {
              "key": "display_name",
              "title": "Description",
              "grow": true,
              "fallback": "description"
            },
            {
              "key": "active",
              "title": "Status",
              "badge": true,
              "width": 110
            },
            {
              "key": "enabled",
              "title": "Startup type",
              "width": 130
            },
            {
              "key": "pid",
              "title": "PID",
              "numeric": true,
              "width": 80
            },
            {
              "key": "start_name",
              "title": "Log on as",
              "width": 190
            }
          ],
          "actions": [
            {
              "id": "start",
              "title": "Start",
              "icon": "play_arrow",
              "tool": "service",
              "params": {
                "name": "{row.name}",
                "state": "started"
              },
              "confirm": true,
              "hide_when": {
                "field": "active",
                "equals": "running"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "stop",
              "title": "Stop",
              "icon": "stop",
              "tool": "service",
              "params": {
                "name": "{row.name}",
                "state": "stopped"
              },
              "confirm": true,
              "hide_when": {
                "field": "active",
                "equals": "stopped"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "restart",
              "title": "Restart",
              "icon": "restart_alt",
              "tool": "service",
              "params": {
                "name": "{row.name}",
                "state": "restarted"
              },
              "confirm": true,
              "hide_when": {
                "field": "active",
                "equals": "stopped"
              }
            }
          ],
          "node_actions": [
            {
              "id": "set-service",
              "title": "Set a service state…",
              "icon": "tune",
              "tool": "service",
              "prefill": {},
              "dry_run_first": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "taskschd",
      "title": "Task Scheduler",
      "mmc_equivalent": "taskschd.msc",
      "icon": "schedule",
      "description": "Every scheduled task on the host — including the several hundred Windows ships itself, because \"which tasks exist here\" has to be answerable in full. The last result is Windows' own code, explained in words rather than reduced to ok/failed.",
